    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **66 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `capacityWarning` flag following the existing pattern for computed, non-persisted response warnings (`bulkSignupWarning`).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `capacityWarning` boolean (read-only, server-derived) to the `OwnerDto` schema, right after `bulkSignupWarning`. This generates the `setCapacityWarning` setter on the generated DTO.\n\n2. **`CapacityWarning.java`** (new) \u2014 A helper mirroring `BulkSignup`. It counts owners already in the same city (case-insensitive), *excluding the owner itself*, and returns `true` when that count is in `[40, 49]`.\n\n3. **`RespondWithOwner.java`** & **`RespondWithOwnerCreated.java`** \u2014 Set `dto.setCapacityWarning(CapacityWarning.warning(owner, ownerRepository))` on both the GET and the create responses.\n\n**Design note:** I made the warning count the *same population* the existing hard check (`CheckOwnerCityCapacity`) uses \u2014 \"other owners already in the city.\" That makes the two rules partition one count cleanly: `40\u201349` warns, `\u226550` is rejected (409). The hard rejection at 50 is untouched, as required. The new `Cp54Tests` passes (fill a city to 40, create the next owner \u2192 `capacityWarning: true`), and the existing capacity/warning/duplicate tests (`Cp18`, `Cp22`, `Cp35`, `Cp10`) and the full suite remain green.",
